data native_test_route_set_form_refuses_universe_underived_on_pristine_main: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "native_test_route_set_form_refuses_universe_underived_on_pristine_main" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**the set-form native test route derives an empty universe on pristine main -- `gunbc test '//pkg:all'` refuses with universe_underived (beside the narrow-pattern artifacts positive_population_empty and required_native_pass_regressed), enumerates zero identities, and per-identity native evidence cannot be produced by any session** (INVALID STATE: the instrument returns 'nothing to run', which reads as success-shaped silence to anything downstream that consumes only the exit status of the required floor; the required floor itself runs claim_executor, so CI stays green while the set-form route is dead).",
    "RECEIPT (2026-10-04, clever-bat-68, main b71e076ed33084d9a1bdbadd75e9ab9ac5bea0ba, remote BuildBuddy job j35cc88f2): `gunbc test '//v2/test/claim/match_binder:all'` with GITHUB_SHA set, bare invocation, seed emit built clean -- exit 2; driver rows carry exactly one lane row (identities=0), [native-occurrence-census] universe=0 observed=0 unobserved=0, file_refusals=0. The same refusal holds on the newer main head bc7838f7b4.",
    "RECEIPT (2026-10-04, clever-bat-68, remote job jeac904a5, one dispatch looping three main-history shas): the rebase base 1b4d5033bf refuses (one file refusal: src/v2/std/node.dag, body_lowering_reason_function_value_body_unread) and still derives an empty universe; a8caab2618 (#13098) refuses with no file refusals at all -- the node.dag refusal is already fixed there, yet the empty universe persists, so the node.dag refusal is NOT the cause; 8102a30f6b refuses with the ingested set collapsed to a pair of paths. The per-sha tallies are re-derivable with the recorded invocation at each sha.",
    "RECEIPT (2026-10-04, clever-bat-68, remote job j9abe886d, four shas looped): the midpoint of the pre-base window (2900bfae77) refuses; e23436ab33 (#13022, advisories counted by identity) refuses; 56a5ab92aa (#13007, StaleBinary refusal) refuses; the 861c829ac6 (#12506) run was killed by the remote runner's 1h free-tier timeout after a clean build (inconclusive). Each result is re-derivable with the recorded invocation at the named sha (remote BuildBuddy dispatch, seed emit clean, bare set-form label). The break is therefore present at or before the midpoint of the 40 first-parent commits in a66665ed93..1b4d5033bf, and in both of the hottest route commits tested from the newer half.",
    "PRE-EXISTING GOOD STATE (2026-10-02, eager-cat-664, head 17fccbf3f62, per the sibling row native_infer_accepts_only_bool_and_int_match_scrutinees's receipt; and 2026-10-03, clever-bat-68, remote jobs j52a3bf42..j95f7798c at a66665ed93): the same invocation derived a non-empty universe (identities=8, closure_modules=15) and enumerated per-identity verdicts in driver-rows.jsonl. The break entered main in the window a66665ed93..1b4d5033bf.",
    "INVARIANCE TO THE FINDER'S OWN CHANGES (2026-10-04, remote jobs jc3e5e428, jf14cc929, j36fcf0ae, jf6c8a28a): the refusal is identical with and without the session's probe-module commit (control at d508aee681), and passing CI's explicit roots to gunbc test (`--source-root dag --source-root src/v2`, the argv the required lane gives claim_executor) exits instantly with status 2 and no driver rows -- wrong argv for the test verb, not a fix.",
    "MECHANISM KNOWN SO FAR: the emitted driver's grammar is `adjudicate <facts> <pattern> <roots...>` (src/v2/compiler/00_compile.dag); the universe is the join of discovery's textual answer (the facts file's discovery.rows, folded over every source through the declared discovery authority), route membership (module namespace starts with v2.test.), and the pattern (extdeps.bazel.target_pattern). Discovery read the whole corpus under the partition telemetry of the rebase base and still produced zero surviving rows, so the break is upstream of pattern matching -- in facts production or the membership join, not in the pattern matcher. In the same window the lane runner itself was heavily reworked -- `git diff a66665ed93 1b4d5033bf -- src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/native_lane_runner.rs src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/required_floor_runner.rs` -- (#13005 route summary, #13007 StaleBinary, #13022 advisories by identity); the driver-side occurrence census and D0-ADJUDICATE machinery are part of that movement.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. Not an OOM or a runner limitation: the lane refuses in seconds after a clean build, on the same machine that built the emitted closure. Not the narrow-pattern artifacts (positive_population_empty, required_native_pass_regressed): those accompany a DERIVED universe on a narrow pattern and were present in the pre-break runs too; universe_underived is the new refusal class. Not stale_binary (#13007): the cause name is universe_underived, and #13007's own head refuses identically. Not the node.dag body-unread refusal (#13010's subject): a8caab2618 has no file refusals at all and still derives universe=0.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: loud-but-blind -- the refusal is typed (exit 2, terminal row, [native-occurrence-census] universe=0 observed=0) yet success-shaped to exit-only consumers, and it masks every per-identity verdict on every branch; no floor lane observes the set-form route's death.",
    "CEILING: structurally decidable. The discovery fold and the membership join are total over the corpus; an empty universe after 7436 corpus reads is a join or production bug with a finite diff to find, not a frontier.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability: a set-form `gunbc test '//v2/test/claim/match_binder:all'` on main again derives a non-empty universe (at least one identity enumerated from discovery rows joined with route membership), adjudicates the pattern's identities, and persists per-identity rows in target/v2-native-lane/driver-rows.jsonl -- the instrument state that a66665ed93 had and main lost.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.witness_v2_native_route", decl_name: "native_route_universe_derived", field: WholeDeclaration },
